==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|stremer}}, {{m|enm|stremere}}, equivalent to {{af|en|stream|-er}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈstɹiːmə(ɹ)/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-streamer.wav |Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːmə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A long, narrow [[flag]], or piece of [[material]] used or seen as a [[decoration]].
#* {{RQ:Dryden Annus Mirabilis|passage=Brave Rupert from afar appears, / Whose waving '''streamers''' the glad general knows.}}
#* {{RQ:Chambers Younger Set|chapter=Afterglow|page=168|passage=Breezes blowing from beds of iris quickened her breath with their perfume; she saw the tufted lilacs sway in the wind, and the '''streamers''' of mauve-tinted wistaria swinging, all a-glisten with golden bees; she saw a crimson cardinal winging through the foliage, and amorous tanagers flashing like scarlet flames athwart the pines.}}
# Strips of paper or other material used as [[confetti]].
# {{lb|en|journalism}} A [[newspaper]] [[headline]] that runs along the top of a [[page]]. <!--may be entire width or just some of the columns-->
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[data]] [[storage]] [[system]], mainly used to produce [[backup]]s, in which large [[quantities]] of data are [[transferred]] to a [[continuously]] [[moving]] [[tape]]; a [[tape drive]].
# {{lb|en|networking}} Any mechanism for [[stream#Verb|stream]]ing data.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=Cevdet Aykanat|author2=Tugrul Dayar|author3=Ibrahim Korpeoglu|title=Computer and Information Sciences - ISCIS 2004: 19th  International Symposium|page=157
|passage=However, integration of a bandwidth estimation algorithm into an adaptive video '''streamer''' is not an easy task. Firstly, bandwidth estimation requires sending extra burst packets that brings a considerable overhead into the system.}}
# {{lb|en|TV|Internet}} A [[subscription]] [[service]] that streams content to an audience.
#: {{cot|en|broadcaster}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/entertainment/archive/2016/02/netflix-ratings/462447/|title=Why Netflix Doesn’t Release Its Ratings|date=2016-02-23|accessdate=2022-11-01|author=Jason Mittell|work=The Atlantic|passage=For starters, the business models for American broadcasters like NBC and '''streamers''' like Netflix (or Hulu, or Amazon) are drastically different.}}
# {{lb|en|internet}} A person who streams activities on their computer (especially video gaming) to a live online audience.
#: {{hyper|en|creator}}
#: {{ux|en|Most '''streamers''' are on Twitch}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Taylor Lorenz|title=In 2020, These Things Came Out on Top|work=The New York Times|date=2020-12-18|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2020/12/18/style/in-2020-these-things-came-out-on-top.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=There was perhaps no group of creators more prepared for the horrors of 2020 than '''streamers'''. Sitting in front of their cameras, often alone, talking for hours to the camera is what they do, and many are excellent at it.}}
# {{lb|en|fishing}} In [[fly fishing]], a variety of [[wet fly]] designed to mimic a [[minnow]].
# {{lb|en|mining}} One who searches for [[stream tin]].
# A stream or column of [[light]] shooting upward from the [[horizon]], constituting one of the forms of the [[aurora borealis]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1888|author={{w|James Russell Lowell}}|title=Heartsease and Rue
|passage=While overhead the North's dumb '''streamers''' shoot.}}
#* {{RQ:Macaulay History of England|passage=The moon was indeed at the full, and the northern '''streamers''' were shining brilliantly.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|education|in combination}} A pupil belonging to a particular stream {{gloss|division by perceived ability}}.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1984|author=Anthony Gale|author2=Antony J. Chapman|title=Psychology and Social Problems|page=82
|passage=Since he also demonstrated that the A-'''streamers''' in his sample showed enhancement of measured intelligence over their primary school careers while the B-'''streamers''' showed deterioration, it can be seen what a far-reaching effect such decisions may have had upon child performance.}}

